# Bank 8 (runs at 0xA000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# THIS BANK HOLDS NO CODE. It is the second half of the sound data: bank 7
# (0x8000) and bank 8 (0xA000) are ALWAYS mapped together (the interrupt does
# it at p00:402C-p00:4032 and the sound trigger at p00:49EF-p00:49FB), so for
# the player they are 16 KB in a row from 0x8000 to 0xBFFF.
#
# That these bytes are the continuation of the sound data is told by the table
# of 80 pointers in bank 7 (0x8328): its last entries point to 0xA034,
# 0xA05D, 0xA09A, ... 0xA3BE, and the last three to 0xA3DE, which is exactly
# the first filler byte. Nobody points here with an address written in an
# instruction, and that is why the table was needed to know it.

B 0xA000 SOUND DATA, SECOND HALF (bank 8)
B 0xA000 Continuation of the data in bank 7. They are indexed by the table of
B 0xA000 80 pointers at 0x8328 (bank 7), which is the one that turns a sound
B 0xA000 number into an address.

D 0xA000 0xA3DE sound_continuation  Melody and effect data, continuing from bank 7. The last fourteen pointers of table 0x8328 land here (0xA034 to 0xA3BE); 0xA3DE is the "empty sound" that the last three entries point to.
F 0xA000 16
D 0xA3DE 0xC000 filler  0xFF filler up to the bank's 8192 bytes.
F 0xA3DE 16
